{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790430316,"nonce":"AgEOSi8Uv17NDhNeiDRzR3bYMUA=","title":"Dict and set shapes: what the runtime leaves for the frontend that registers them","message":"The generator (dicts.rs, dict_declarations/set_declarations) gives each shape find_any, contains_any, get_any, del_any, eq_any and from_dyn, and the dynamic layer routes boxes of a shape's kind to zb_hook_shaped_{getitem,setitem,delitem,contains,len,eq,hash,json} (stubbed in zypy and zylua). Not done:\n\n- Ordering of boxed shaped sets (zb_any_lt/zb_any_le take only SET_TAG sets) and set arithmetic on boxed shaped sets (zb_any_set_arith).\n- Method calls on a boxed shaped dict or set (classes.rs builtin_arms lists DICT_TAG and SET_TAG only); zb_hook_shaped_items and zb_hook_shaped_repr need the shapes' arms too.\n- A static probe of a typed shape by a key of another typed kind (dict_probe_by covers probes into the dynamic shape only); find_any has the rule for dynamic keys, including element-wise tuples through boxed comparison.\n- A delete loop's rebuild count has no trace switch; compaction runs when the dead outnumber half the live, which bounds it by log n.","files":null}]}